  "context_pill": "Section 115BAC Tax Liability & Section 87A Rebate",
  "example_summary": "Tax Computation for Mr. Mahesh under Section 115BAC",
  "source_provision": "### Statutory Slabs & Tax Rates u/s 115BAC (Default Tax Regime)\n\n| Total Income Slab | Applicable Tax Rate |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| Up to ₹ 4,00,000 | **Nil** |\n| ₹ 4,00,001 — ₹ 8,00,000 | **5%** |\n| ₹ 8,00,001 — ₹ 12,00,000 | **10%** |\n| ₹ 12,00,001 — ₹ 16,00,000 | **15%** |\n| ₹ 16,00,001 — ₹ 20,00,000 | **20%** |\n| ₹ 20,00,001 — ₹ 24,00,000 | **25%** |\n| Above ₹ 24,00,000 | **30%** |\n\n\n### Core Statutory Conditions Checklist\n\n- **Section 115BAC Default Regime**: Applicable automatically to Individuals, HUFs, AOPs, BOIs, and AJPs unless an explicit option to opt out under Section 115BAC(6) is exercised.\n- **Section 87A Rebate Eligibility**: Restricted exclusively to a **Resident Individual** whose Total Income does not exceed **₹ 12,00,000** under the default tax regime.\n- **Maximum Rebate Limit**: Quantum of rebate is **100% of income tax payable** or **₹ 60,000**, whichever is lower.\n\n\n> [!IMPORTANT] Marginal Relief u/s 87A\n> Where Total Income marginally exceeds ₹ 12,00,000 under Section 115BAC, marginal relief ensures that the net tax payable shall not exceed the Total Income in excess of ₹ 12,00,000.",
